⍝ ZZ74_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ Faults in the construction of the 3-line error display, in
      ⍝ particular for statements that were optimized by the parser.
      ⍝





      ⍝ a defined function with a multi-line string: the lines of the body
      ⍝ are no longer the lines of the function text. reparse() used the
      ⍝ text of the wrong line (here: abc) for an optimized statement.
      ⍝
      ∇Z←MLS B
      Z←"""
      abc
      """
      Z←Z+2 3⍴1
      ∇





      MLS 1
DOMAIN ERROR
MLS[2]  Z←Z+2 3⍴1
          ^^





      )SIC





      ⍝ the same for a comment line, which has no tokens in the body
      ⍝
      ∇Z←CMT B
      ⍝ a comment
      Z←(2 2⍴1)+1 2 3
      ∇





      CMT 1
RANK ERROR+
CMT[2]  Z←(2 2⍴1)+1 2 3
          ^      ^





      )SIC





      ⍝ a conditional statement C →→ T ←→ F ←← is one statement in the text,
      ⍝ but its segments C, T, and F are statements of their own in the body.
      ⍝ For an optimized segment, line 2 showed the entire statement with
      ⍝ the carets of the segment.
      ⍝
      0 →→ 'T' ←→ (2 2⍴1)+1 2 3 ←←
RANK ERROR+
      (2 2⍴1)+1 2 3
      ^      ^





      1 →→ (2 2⍴1)+1 2 3 ←→ 'F' ←←
RANK ERROR+
      (2 2⍴1)+1 2 3
      ^      ^





      ⍝ a folded ⊂B has 2 tokens (not 3 as a folded A⍴B), and repeated folds
      ⍝ (⊂⊂B, A⍴⊂B) are one value. Counting 3 tokens for every fold put the
      ⍝ carets left of it one token off.
      ⍝
      'a'+(⊂1 2)
DOMAIN ERROR
      'a'+(⊂1 2)
      ^  ^





      'a'+⊂⊂1 2
DOMAIN ERROR
      'a'+⊂⊂1 2
      ^  ^





      'a'+2 2⍴⊂1 2
DOMAIN ERROR
      'a'+2 2⍴⊂1 2
      ^  ^





      X←3 ◊ (X ⊂ ⊂1 2)+'a'
RANK ERROR+
      (X⊂⊂1 2)+'a'
       ^^





      ⍝ the macro of a derived function reports the whole statement: its
      ⍝ range ended at the END token, which has no counterpart in the
      ⍝ unoptimized statement
      ⍝
      (⍳⍤1) 2 2⍴'ab'
DOMAIN ERROR
      (⍳⍤1)2 2⍴'ab'
      ^    ^





      )SIC





      ⍝ a folded value (2⍴1) together with a merged ⊤∧ (2 tokens, 1 in the
      ⍝ optimized body): the carets are placed by the PCs of the Token_locs
      ⍝ (the positions of the tokens in the original token string of the
      ⍝ line) and are therefore not shifted by the optimizations.
      ⍝
      1 2 3 4 + (2⍴1)⊤∧1 2 3
LENGTH ERROR+
      1 2 3 4+(2⍴1)⊤∧1 2 3
              ^    ^





      )SIC





      1 2 3 4 + 1 0 1⊤∧(2⍴1)
LENGTH ERROR+
      1 2 3 4+1 0 1⊤∧(2⍴1)
              ^    ^





      )SIC





      ⍝ Bugs35 #4: a folded ⊂B that is also folded by monadic , or ⍪
      ⍝ (and A⍴B or ⊂⊂B under ,): the left caret is under the ( as
      ⍝ entered, not one token further right.
      ⍝





      X←(,⊂'abc')+1
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(,⊂'abc')+1
        ^        ^


      )SIC





      X←(⍪⊂'abc')+1
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(⍪⊂'abc')+1
        ^        ^


      )SIC





      X←1 2+(,⊂'ab'),1 2 3
LENGTH ERROR+
      X←1 2+(,⊂'ab'),1 2 3
        ^  ^


      )SIC





      X←(,2 2⍴'abcd')+1
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(,2 2⍴'abcd')+1
        ^            ^


      )SIC





      X←(,⊂⊂'abc')+1
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(,⊂⊂'abc')+1
        ^         ^


      )SIC





      ⍝ Bugs35 #5: a one-character literal before an unbalanced ) or ]
      ⍝ was displayed as VALUE ERROR (with a stale line 2).
      ⍝





      'a'◊2)
Unbalanced right parenthesis+
      'a'◊2)
           ^


      X←'a' ◊ 2)
Unbalanced right parenthesis+
      X←'a'◊2)
             ^


      'a' ◊ 2]
Unbalanced right square bracket+
      'a'◊2]
           ^


      ⍝ Bugs35 #6: an empty statement or a conditional statement before
      ⍝ the failed one: line 2 shows the statement as entered, not the
      ⍝ optimized body.
      ⍝





       ◊ X←(2 2⍴7)+1 2 3
RANK ERROR+
      X←(2 2⍴7)+1 2 3
        ^      ^


      )SIC





      1 ◊ ◊ X←(⊂'ab')+1 2 3
1
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(⊂'ab')+1 2 3
        ^      ^

      )SIC





      X←1 →→ 2 ←→ 3 ←← ◊ Z←(2 2⍴7)+1 2 3
2
RANK ERROR+
      Z←(2 2⍴7)+1 2 3
        ^      ^

      )SIC





      ⍎' ◊ X←(⊂''ab'')+1 2 3'
DOMAIN ERROR
      X←(⊂'ab')+1 2 3
        ^      ^


      )SIC





      ⍝ Bugs35 #51: line 2 shows the canonical form (APL input format) of
      ⍝ the parsed statement: a parenthesized group that the parser has
      ⍝ folded into one value keeps its parentheses where they matter, e.g.
      ⍝ (1 2) (3 4 5) or (1 2 3)[2], and loses redundant ones, e.g. (1 2)+3.
      ⍝





      ⊣⎕FX 'F51' '(1 2)+1 2 3'





      F51
LENGTH ERROR+
F51[1]  1 2+1 2 3
        ^  ^


      )SIC





      1 (2) 3+'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      1 2 3+'a'
      ^    ^


      )SIC





      (1)+'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      1+'a'
      ^^


      )SIC





      (1 2)(3 4 5)+1 2 3
LENGTH ERROR+
      (1 2) (3 4 5)+1 2 3
      ^            ^

      )SIC





      A←5





      A (1 2)+'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      A(1 2)+'a'
      ^     ^





      )SIC





      (1 2) A+'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      (1 2)A+'a'
      ^     ^





      )SIC





      (1 2 3)[4]
INDEX ERROR+
      (1 2 3)[4]
      ^      ^





      )SIC





      ⍝ Bugs35 #51 (cont.): numbers in line 2 have full precision (they
      ⍝ were shown with ⎕PP 10), other tokens their canonical form
      ⍝ (ρ → ⍴, * → ⋆).
      ⍝





      1   ((2 3))   4 5                  ÷ 0
DOMAIN ERROR
      1 (2 3) 4 5÷0
      ^          ^





      )SIC





      1.50 ÷ 0
DOMAIN ERROR
      1.5÷0
      ^  ^





      )SIC





      3.14159265358979 1E10 00.250e05J1.0+'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      3.14159265358979 10000000000 25000J1+'a'
      ^                                   ^





      )SIC





      2 3ρ*'a'
DOMAIN ERROR
      2 3⍴⋆'a'
          ^





      )SIC





      ⍝ PR_APL_FUN (1 ⎕CR, error line 2) is the APL input format: the
      ⍝ shortest text that ⍎ turns into an identical value, with full
      ⍝ precision (⎕PP is ignored). It lost ranks, shapes, and enclosures.
      ⍝





      ⎕PP←5





      1 ⎕CR 3.14159265358979
3.14159265358979





      1 ⎕CR ,'a'
,'a'





      1 ⎕CR ,5
,5





      1 ⎕CR ⊂1 2
⊂1 2





      1 ⎕CR 2 2⍴⍳4
2 2⍴1 2 3 4





      1 ⎕CR 1 (⊂1 2)
1 (⊂1 2)





      1 ⎕CR (,1) 2
(,1) 2





      1 ⎕CR 0⍴⊂1 2
0⍴⊂0 0





      1 ⎕CR 1E¯5 1J2 ¯2
1E¯5 1J2 ¯2





      1 ⎕CR 'it''s' ⍬ (2 2⍴'abcd')
'it''s' ⍬ (2 2⍴'abcd')





      ⎕PP←10





